## Pinned upstream sources for the vendored drop-in files under lib/. SHCL
## ships as one self-contained file per language, so it is copied in rather than
## required as a module: that keeps this program at standard library plus its own
## source, and keeps the go directive off upstream's (higher) floor. The cost of
## copying is that drift is invisible, which is what the pin plus
## utility/check-vendor.bash buys back.
##
## One line per vendored file:  LOCAL_PATH|OWNER/REPO|REF|PATH_IN_UPSTREAM
## LOCAL_PATH is relative to the repo root. REF is what the copy was taken from:
## a release tag, or a full 40-character commit SHA for an unreleased build. A
## SHA pin prints a pre-release notice on every run, so it gets moved to a tag
## once one exists. Bump REF in the same commit that refreshes the file.
##
## shcl is on its unreleased 3.0 dev tree on purpose, until 3.0.0 is tagged.
VENDOR_PINS=(
	"lib/shcl/shcl.go|yottacore/shcl|f8e27a222718138f644b606771fa1fbf6fb7e4e3|source/go/shcl.go"
)
